%U A400229 3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3
%N A400229 The sequence of side-lengths that occur when drawing a sequence of squares in the plane with integer side lengths such that the bottom-left corner of the k-th square is at the nonnegative integer point (k, y_k), subject to the conditions that (1) the interior of each square has a distinct pattern made by the perimeters of the other squares, and (2) the sequence (a(0), y_0, a(1), y_1, a(2), y_2, ...) is the lexicographically earliest such infinite sequence.
%H A400229 Peter Kagey, <a href="https://codegolf.stackexchange.com/q/291882/53884">The Eternal Internal Patterns of Squares</a>, Code Golf Stack Exchange.
%e A400229 The sequence of squares where the first square has side length a(0)=1, and y-value A400230(0)=0; the next has side length a(1)=2 and y-value A400230(1)=0; and so on. The index of each square is marked in the lower right corner, where A=10, B=11, and C=12.
